  "name": "Conveyor rule fixture",
  "conveyor_simulation_mode": "logical",
  "_comment": "Not a showcase. Two independent lines that between them reach the transport rules the shipped stations do not. The dead-end line proves rule 12 - a conveyor whose downstream interface touches nothing stops its products at progress 1 instead of deleting them - and its spawner carries maxActiveSpawns, so the three stopped products must also hold the cap closed for the rest of the run; a port that deletes at a disconnected end frees the cap and spawns forever, which is a divergence of hundreds of lines rather than a rounding difference. The sink line is the control: the same cadence with a deleter downstream, which must keep retiring products and keep spawning. Deliberately no robot, so nothing but the conveyor rules moves anything.",
